    "https://jobs.nicholls.edu/postings/10256": {
      "title": "Instructor of Nursing",
      "description": "Nicholls State University Portal | Instructor of Nursing Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Instructor of Nursing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Special Instructions Nicholls State University adheres to the equal opportunity provisions of federal civil rights laws and regulations that are applicable to this agency. Therefore, no one will be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, national origin (Title VI of the Civil Rights Act of 1964); sex (Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972); disability (Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973; or age (Age Discrimination Act of 1975) in attaining educational goals and objectives and in the administration of personnel policies and procedures. Anyone with questions regarding this policy may contact Alison Hadaway, SHRM -CP, Director of Human Resources at 985-448-4041 / alison.hadaway@nicholls.edu / P.O. Box 2105, Thibodaux, LA 70310. For anyone needing ADA Accommodations, please contact Carolyn Kern, Director of Environmental Health & Safety at 985-448-4782 / carolyn.kern@nicholls.edu Position Details Position Information Position Title Instructor of Nursing Position Number 187937 Salary Range $55,000.00 Position Type Faculty Department Information Ending Effective Date of Temporary Employment Department Nursing Job Duties Responsibility / Duty Responsibilities include classroom, laboratory, and clinical teaching in the Bachelor of Science in Nursing Program and/or the MSN Program, as applicable. Instruction occurs in a vibrant, technology-enhanced learning environment. A successful candidate must be professional, engaging, collegial, and function as a team member aligned to the educational principles of the programs of study. As both programs are CCNE accredited, each faculty member is responsible and accountable to fully engage in program assessment, and in particular, the systematic plan for program evaluation, as a shared and collective voice. Percentage Of Time 80 Responsibility / Duty Responsibilities include service to the University, College, Department, Program, the community, and beyond. Service is integral and includes key functions such as advising and mentoring students, providing service in the form of committee work at all levels both internal and external to the University and Department, professional organizations, leading groups, and more. Percentage Of Time 10 Responsibility / Duty Responsibilities include service to the University, College, Department, Program, the community, and beyond. Service is integral and includes key functions such as advising and mentoring students, providing service in the form of committee work at all levels both internal and external to the University and Department, professional organizations, leading groups, and more. Percentage Of Time 10 Posting Detail Information Minimum Experience Required 2 years of RN clinical experience Minimum Education Required MSN or MN Minimum Licenses Required Current unencumbered/unrestricted Louisiana RN license, and/or APRN license Other Minimum Requirements BLS Test(s) Required Preferred Education FNP or Doctoral prepared Preferred Experience Adult Health Preferred Licenses Other Preferred Requirements Physical Demands Fit for duty in clinical and lab settings Employment Year Academic Year If Grant Period or Specified Period selected, please specify begin date If Grant Period or Specified Period selected, please specify end date Employment Basis Full-time Proposed Ending Date (for faculty and grant funded positions) 05/15/2027 Posting Date 05/19/2026 Closing Date 12/31/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Postings https://jobs.nicholls.edu/postings/9895 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Teaching Philosophy Names and Contact Information for a Minimum of THREE References Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Copy of Transcript Optional Documents Other Document 906 East 1st Street, Thibodaux, LA 70301 Back to top Copyright © PeopleAdmin To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
