    "https://jobs.nicholls.edu/postings/10402": {
      "title": "Instructor of Allied Health Sciences",
      "description": "Nicholls State University Portal | Instructor of Allied Health Sciences Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Instructor of Allied Health Sciences Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Special Instructions Nicholls State University adheres to the equal opportunity provisions of federal civil rights laws and regulations that are applicable to this agency. Therefore, no one will be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, national origin (Title VI of the Civil Rights Act of 1964); sex (Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972); disability (Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973; or age (Age Discrimination Act of 1975) in attaining educational goals and objectives and in the administration of personnel policies and procedures. Anyone with questions regarding this policy may contact Alison Hadaway, SHRM -CP, Director of Human Resources at 985-448-4041 / alison.hadaway@nicholls.edu / P.O. Box 2105, Thibodaux, LA 70310. For anyone needing ADA Accommodations, please contact Carolyn Kern, Director of Environmental Health & Safety at 985-448-4782 / carolyn.kern@nicholls.edu Position Details Position Information Position Title Instructor of Allied Health Sciences Position Number 500239 Salary Range $47,893.00 Position Type Faculty Department Information Ending Effective Date of Temporary Employment Department Allied Health Sciences Job Duties Responsibility / Duty Faculty must teach 15 contact hours, maintain 10 office hours, and be available for department service and functions. Teach upper and lower level courses related to Allied Health Sciences. Percentage Of Time 80 Responsibility / Duty Participate in departmental recruitment and retention efforts. Participate in other acts of service to the University, College, Department, Profession and the community. Contribute to scholarship in the professional discipline. Accountable for ensuring the affirmative action, equal opportunity, and diversity are integrally tied to all actions and decisions in areas of responsibility. Percentage Of Time 20 Posting Detail Information Minimum Experience Required Two years of clinical experience. Teaching experience. Minimum Education Required Masters or Ph.D in an Allied Health related field Minimum Licenses Required Credentialed professional in the discipline and current license to practice in Louisiana, if applicable. Other Minimum Requirements Maintenance and documentation of current knowledge and skills in areas of responsibility. The candidate must be self-motivated, student-oriented, and willing to be a successful academic advisor. Test(s) Required Preferred Education Masters or Ph.D in an Allied Health related field Preferred Experience Clinical experience in an Allied Health related field Preferred Licenses Credentialed professional in the discipline and current license to practice in Louisiana, if applicable. Other Preferred Requirements Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively and effectively with department head, program coordinator, other faculty, and staff. Demonstrates compassionate and effective communication skills to advise students. Physical Demands Employment Year Academic Year If Grant Period or Specified Period selected, please specify begin date If Grant Period or Specified Period selected, please specify end date Employment Basis Full-time Proposed Ending Date (for faculty and grant funded positions) Posting Date 08/16/2026 Closing Date 09/18/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Postings https://jobs.nicholls.edu/postings/10336 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Teaching Philosophy Names and Contact Information for a Minimum of THREE References Copy of Transcript Optional Documents Other Document 906 East 1st Street, Thibodaux, LA 70301 Back to top Copyright © PeopleAdmin To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
