    "https://jobs.nicholls.edu/postings/10408": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "Nicholls State University Portal | Digital Resources Management &amp; Acquisitions Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Digital Resources Management & Acquisitions Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Special Instructions Nicholls State University adheres to the equal opportunity provisions of federal civil rights laws and regulations that are applicable to this agency. Therefore, no one will be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, national origin (Title VI of the Civil Rights Act of 1964); sex (Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972); disability (Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973; or age (Age Discrimination Act of 1975) in attaining educational goals and objectives and in the administration of personnel policies and procedures. Anyone with questions regarding this policy may contact Alison Hadaway, SHRM -CP, Director of Human Resources at 985-448-4041 / alison.hadaway@nicholls.edu / P.O. Box 2105, Thibodaux, LA 70310. For anyone needing ADA Accommodations, please contact Carolyn Kern, Director of Environmental Health & Safety at 985-448-4782 / carolyn.kern@nicholls.edu Position Details Position Information Position Title Digital Resources Management & Acquisitions Position Number 134553 Salary Range $40,000.00 Position Type Unclassified Staff Department Information Ending Effective Date of Temporary Employment Department University Library Job Duties Responsibility / Duty Load electronic resources into the library’s catalog system as they are purchased. Performs copy cataloging and assists with other aspects of technical services. Performs basic collection management duties such as preparation, repair, and deaccessioning materials. Act as a service contact for equipment, tools, and software for the maintenance of digital collections, such as printers and scanners. Participate in annual reporting by collecting and sharing statistical and other data as instructed. Maintain administrative account information and documentation for vendors and electronic resources. Performs library acquisitions duties as necessary including placing orders, contacting vendors, receiving orders, handling invoices, inputting and editing new records for items on order. Percentage Of Time 50 Responsibility / Duty ● Acts as a LOUIS System Administrator Backup and perform all duties that come with the title ● Assists library patrons with computer and online resource related issues; assist library staff with computer hardware and software issues; involve campus IT as needed ● Assists the Head of Access Services in maintaining the library’s laptop lending program by monitoring device inventory, troubleshooting issues, and using fleet management software to track and remotely secure devices as necessary. ● Assists Information Technology Technical Support Analyst with annual inventory report. Percentage Of Time 35 Responsibility / Duty Assists with promoting Affordable Learning, facilitates e-textbook adoptions from the library’s collection, and collects data for campus adoptions. Complete special project work as assigned including record enhancement, clean up, or reclassification. Percentage Of Time 10 Responsibility / Duty Serves as backup for the public services area of circulation and keeps current with the policies and procedures of this area. Participates in library committees and may participate in university committees and/or national and regional professional organizations as appropriate. Assumes other responsibilities as required. Percentage Of Time 5 Posting Detail Information Minimum Experience Required ● Bachelor’s degree from a regionally accredited college or university, or at least four years of extensive library experience. ● Extensive experience with spreadsheets. ● Ability to communicate effectively orally and in writing. Minimum Education Required A baccalaureate degree. Minimum Licenses Required Other Minimum Requirements Test(s) Required Preferred Education Preferred Experience ● Library technical services experience (Experience with using OCLC and Alma) ● Experience collecting and compiling data. ● Experience in an academic setting. Preferred Licenses Other Preferred Requirements Physical Demands Employment Year Fiscal Year If Grant Period or Specified Period selected, please specify begin date If Grant Period or Specified Period selected, please specify end date Employment Basis Full-time Proposed Ending Date (for faculty and grant funded positions) Posting Date 09/04/2026 Closing Date 09/18/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Postings https://jobs.nicholls.edu/postings/10407 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Names and Contact Information for a Minimum of THREE References Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Optional Documents Other Document 906 East 1st Street, Thibodaux, LA 70301 Back to top Copyright © PeopleAdmin To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
