    "https://jobs.nicholls.edu/postings/10430": {
      "title": "Nicholls State University Portal",
      "description": "Nicholls State University Portal | Custodian 1 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Custodian 1 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Special Instructions Nicholls State University adheres to the equal opportunity provisions of federal civil rights laws and regulations that are applicable to this agency. Therefore, no one will be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, national origin (Title VI of the Civil Rights Act of 1964); sex (Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972); disability (Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973; or age (Age Discrimination Act of 1975) in attaining educational goals and objectives and in the administration of personnel policies and procedures. Anyone with questions regarding this policy may contact Alison Hadaway, SHRM -CP, Director of Human Resources at 985-448-4041 / alison.hadaway@nicholls.edu / P.O. Box 2105, Thibodaux, LA 70310. For anyone needing ADA Accommodations, please contact Carolyn Kern, Director of Environmental Health & Safety at 985-448-4782 / carolyn.kern@nicholls.edu Position Details Position Information Position Title Custodian 1 Position Number 029041 Salary Range $20,800.00 - $37,440.00 Hires at Minimum Position Type Classified Staff Department Information Ending Effective Date of Temporary Employment Department Student Union Job Duties Responsibility / Duty Function of Work: Performs a variety of duties n the Student Union including, but not limited to, setup of meeting rooms for meetings and events. Custodial duties, and various facility maintenance tasks. Custodial Functions: Performs custodial related duties necessary to maintain cleanliness and sanitary conditions in Student Union common areas, offices, conference facilities, all restrooms, Ballroom, the Century Room, 3rd floor of the press box in football stadium, and other areas as assigned by supervisor. Sweeps sidewalks, porches, and tiled surfaces. Operates wet/dry vacuum for cleaning and shampooing carpeted areas. Cleans and waxes floors using industrial size mops and/or machines. Mixes or blends routine cleaning solutions to proper concentrations as necessary for various tasks. Strips and polishes floors using buffing machines. Washes blinds, windows, and walls with prescribed solutions. Empties and decontaminates trash containers. Percentage Of Time 45 Responsibility / Duty Faculty/Event Setup: Sets up and takes down tables and chairs for events in meeting facilities (such as ballroom, Bollinger suite, snack bar area). Operates heavy life equipment in the Union using proper safety protocol. Transports equipment/resources to other campus locations such as the Century Room. Moves, rearranges, cleans and dusts furniture and fixtures. Percentage Of Time 40 Responsibility / Duty Facility Maintenance: Paints interior and exterior surfaces when necessary and directed by supervisor. Performs many varied tasks necessary for the upkeep of buildings and grounds. Percentage Of Time 10 Responsibility / Duty Other duties as assigned Percentage Of Time 5 Posting Detail Information Minimum Experience Required MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS : No experience or training required. Minimum Education Required Minimum Licenses Required Other Minimum Requirements Applicants must complete the application in its entirety with an electronic signature and date. ****Resumes will not be accepted as a substitute for the application.**** If employment history is not completed, the application will be disqualified. Please include any current and previous employment at Nicholls State University. Personnel files are not pulled for application purposes. Test(s) Required No Test Required. Preferred Education Preferred Experience Preferred Licenses Other Preferred Requirements Physical Demands Employment Year Fiscal Year If Grant Period or Specified Period selected, please specify begin date If Grant Period or Specified Period selected, please specify end date Employment Basis Full-time Proposed Ending Date (for faculty and grant funded positions) Posting Date 09/14/2026 Closing Date 09/24/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Postings https://jobs.nicholls.edu/postings/10383 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Other Document Other Document 906 East 1st Street, Thibodaux, LA 70301 Back to top Copyright © PeopleAdmin To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.nicholls.edu/postings/10434": {
      "title": "STCW Clerk and Sea Project Specialist",
      "description": "Nicholls State University Portal | STCW Clerk and Sea Project Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help STCW Clerk and Sea Project Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Special Instructions Nicholls State University adheres to the equal opportunity provisions of federal civil rights laws and regulations that are applicable to this agency. Therefore, no one will be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, national origin (Title VI of the Civil Rights Act of 1964); sex (Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972); disability (Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973; or age (Age Discrimination Act of 1975) in attaining educational goals and objectives and in the administration of personnel policies and procedures. Anyone with questions regarding this policy may contact Alison Hadaway, SHRM -CP, Director of Human Resources at 985-448-4041 / alison.hadaway@nicholls.edu / P.O. Box 2105, Thibodaux, LA 70310. For anyone needing ADA Accommodations, please contact Carolyn Kern, Director of Environmental Health & Safety at 985-448-4782 / carolyn.kern@nicholls.edu Position Details Position Information Position Title STCW Clerk and Sea Project Specialist Position Number 500264 Salary Range $59,000-$66,000 Position Type Unclassified Staff Department Information Ending Effective Date of Temporary Employment Department Office of the President Job Duties Responsibility / Duty Government and Industry Liaison – 50% Serves as liaison to MARAD , the USCG National Maritime Center ( USCG NMC ), and other applicable USCG Divisions in order to remain current with respect to applicable laws, USCG polices, and international treaties which apply to merchant mariner credentialing; continuously seeks ways to improve the Academy&#39;s credentialing processes and ensure a positive rapport with: MARAD , USCG , and NMC . Serves as liaison with Offshore, Towing and Ocean shipping companies, arranging for berths on designated vessels, arranging time and place to board, and providing required information on each cadet. Obtains commercial berths for cadet sea projects, as well as, completes all logistics for cadets assigned sea projects. Academy representative on USCG and MARAD working groups and required to maintain a working relationship with other maritime academy STCW Clerk/ Sea Project staff. Coordinates all interactions with the U.S. Navy’s Military Sealift Command including all logistics for annual recruiting visits. Required to attend annual STCW Coordinator meeting at USCG National Maritime Center. Maintain contact with USCG through the credentialing process. Represent the Maritime Academy at local and national events to establish and strengthen relationships Percentage Of Time 50 Responsibility / Duty Regulatory Approval &amp; Compliance – 40% Processes all cadet applications for USCG merchant mariner credentials and USCG medical certificates, make arrangements for the USCG license exams for senior cadets. Ensures proper documentation is supplied by each cadet per individual company requirements such as physicals, drug tests, immunizations and applications. Oversees all logistical requirements for cadet sea projects. Manage Sea Project homework submission, scans and performs data entry of all documentation (federal documents- TWIC , USCG , Merchant Mariner Credential and USCG health certificate). Ensures all requirements are met prior to issuance of a Merchant Mariner Credential with an officer endorsement (degree audit, no holds, flashing light, etc.). Ensures proper documentation is supplied for each cadet per academy requirements such as registration, insurance coverage, homework assignments plus discharges, letters of recommendation and officer evaluations when cadets return from ships. Percentage Of Time 40 Responsibility / Duty Instructional Quality &amp; Program Assessment – 10% Maintain cadet files in accordance with USCG requirements and ensure they are audit ready. Works closely with the Registrar regarding documentation of USCG and academic graduation requirements. Specifically ensuring new students obtain USCG documents and have internships on commercial vessels. Responsible for ensuring that all cadet internships are with companies that meet U.S. Maritime Administration and LMA Sexual Assault/ Sexual Harassment (SA / SH) policy requirements, and that cadets complete required SA/ SH training prior to departing for an internship on a commercial vessel. May supervise supplemental and student employees as needed. Percentage Of Time 10 Posting Detail Information Minimum Experience Required Between 1-2 years of related maritime experience (Required) Two years of administrative experience (Required) Two years of experience with legal guidelines and policy compliance (Required) Minimum Education Required Minimum Licenses Required Other Minimum Requirements In-depth knowledge of the Merchant Marine Industry (Required) Demonstrated knowledge of STCW requirements, U.S. Coast Guard regulations, and credentialing standards relevant to maritime training. Test(s) Required Preferred Education Bachelor’s Degree (Not Required) Preferred Experience Preferred Licenses Valid Transportation Worker Identification Credential Card obtained in the first 6 months of employment (Required) Notary Public (Not Required) Ability to maintain a database (Required) Ability to maintain individual files for each cadet that are subject to audit (Required) Other Preferred Requirements Physical Demands Employment Year Fiscal Year If Grant Period or Specified Period selected, please specify begin date If Grant Period or Specified Period selected, please specify end date Employment Basis Full-time Proposed Ending Date (for faculty and grant funded positions) Posting Date 09/14/2026 Closing Date 10/13/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Postings https://jobs.nicholls.edu/postings/10433 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume/CV Names and Contact Information for a Minimum of THREE References Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Copy of Transcript Optional Documents Other Document 906 East 1st Street, Thibodaux, LA 70301 Back to top Copyright © PeopleAdmin To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.nicholls.edu/postings/10431": {
      "title": "Nicholls State University Portal",
      "description": "Nicholls State University Portal | Police Sergeant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Police Sergeant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Special Instructions Nicholls State University adheres to the equal opportunity provisions of federal civil rights laws and regulations that are applicable to this agency. Therefore, no one will be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, national origin (Title VI of the Civil Rights Act of 1964); sex (Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972); disability (Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973; or age (Age Discrimination Act of 1975) in attaining educational goals and objectives and in the administration of personnel policies and procedures. Anyone with questions regarding this policy may contact Alison Hadaway, SHRM -CP, Director of Human Resources at 985-448-4041 / alison.hadaway@nicholls.edu / P.O. Box 2105, Thibodaux, LA 70310. For anyone needing ADA Accommodations, please contact Carolyn Kern, Director of Environmental Health & Safety at 985-448-4782 / carolyn.kern@nicholls.edu Position Details Position Information Position Title Police Sergeant Position Number 500234 Salary Range $50,648.00 Special Entrance Rate - $92,851.00 Hires at Minimum Rate Position Type Classified Staff Department Information Ending Effective Date of Temporary Employment Department University Police Job Duties Responsibility / Duty Function of Work: To protect lives and property by conducting foot and mobile security patrols; enforcing parking and traffic regulations; rendering emergency services; investigating crimes and making arrest when necessary. Provides a wide range of police services. Performs all the duties required of lower-level officers as necessary. Percentage Of Time 30 Responsibility / Duty Oversees and evaluates performance of lower-level officers on an assigned shift. Percentage Of Time 20 Responsibility / Duty Reviews and signs all reports submitted by lower-level officers. Percentage Of Time 20 Responsibility / Duty Conducts roll call and officer, vehicle, and equipment inspections. Percentage Of Time 10 Responsibility / Duty Serves as training officer by planning and coordinating training programs. Percentage Of Time 10 Responsibility / Duty Maintains firearms, armory, and other equipment. Percentage Of Time 10 Posting Detail Information Minimum Experience Required MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS : Three years of law enforcement experience. EXPERIENCE SUBSTITUTION : Every 30 semester hours earned from an accredited college or university will substitute for one year of the required experience. The maximum substitution allowed is 60 semester hours which substitutes for two years of experience. NECESSARY SPECIAL REQUIREMENTS : Applicants must be at least 18 years of age. Possession of a valid Louisiana driver’s license. Possession of an active Peace Officer Standards and Training ( POST ) certification may be required. An applicant who has been convicted of a felony or who is under indictment on a felony charge will be disqualified until relief from the disabilities imposed by state and federal laws is granted. Minimum Education Required High School diploma or equivalent. Minimum Licenses Required Other Minimum Requirements Applicants must complete the application in its entirety with an electronic signature and date. ****Resumes will not be accepted as a substitute for the application.**** If education and employment history are not completed, the application will be disqualified. When listing Job Duties, please include if you are Commissioned with the Power of Arrest. ****Please include any current and previous employment at Nicholls State University. Personnel files are not pulled for application purposes.**** Applicants claiming education as a substitution for work experience must have their Official College Transcripts delivered to the Human Resources Department at hr@nicholls.edu or emailed directly to Jennifer.Prejean@nicholls.edu prior to the job closing date. Unofficial transcripts are NOT accepted. Test(s) Required Applicants must have an active 2100- PSE (Protective Services Exam) score by the time the posting closes in order to be considered for the position unless exempted by Civil Service rule or policy or meets one of the following testing exemptions: 1)An applicant who meets the Minimum Qualifications and has a Peace Officer Standards and Training ( POST ) certification from a Louisiana accredited training academy may be appointed by probational appointment or job appointment to a job which requires the Protective Services Exam without a test score. The applicant’s POST certification shall not be under suspension or pending a revocation hearing OR 2)A veteran of the armed forces who served at least 90 days of active duty for purposes other than training and who has been honorably discharged from active duty within the previous twelve months. (DD214 must be attached to application or submitted to Human Resources by fax or mail by the closing date of the announcement). Applicants claiming testing exemption must have the appropriate documentation listed above attached to the application or contact Jennifer Prejean in Human Resources by the closing date via phone 985-493-2679 or email Jennifer.Prejean@nicholls.edu For more information on Civil Service testing, please follow the link below: https://jobs.la.gov/TestInformation/TestingProcess.aspx Preferred Education Preferred Experience Preferred Licenses Other Preferred Requirements Physical Demands This position requires the ability to work shift work (days, nights, weekends, and Holidays). Physical Demands and/or Unavoidable Hazards of the Position In this position you may be required to: -stand or be on your feet for long periods of time; -work in/be outside during inclement weather; -carry heavy objects (50-100lbs) -subjected to loud noises -may be required to use and qualify with firearms; -must be able to run, crawl, stoop, squat, kneel as necessary Employment Year Fiscal Year If Grant Period or Specified Period selected, please specify begin date If Grant Period or Specified Period selected, please specify end date Employment Basis Full-time Proposed Ending Date (for faculty and grant funded positions) Posting Date 09/14/2026 Closing Date 09/24/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Postings https://jobs.nicholls.edu/postings/9878 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you taken the Civil Service Protective Service Exam 2100-PSE? Yes No * Are you POST Certified? Yes No * Do you have your POST Certificate? If YES, please download a copy as \"Other Document\" in the Documents Needed to Apply section of the application or email directly to jennifer.prejean@nicholls.edu. Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Copy of Transcript Other Document Other Document 906 East 1st Street, Thibodaux, LA 70301 Back to top Copyright © PeopleAdmin To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.nicholls.edu/postings/10439": {
      "title": "STCW Clerk and Sea Project Specialist",
      "description": "Nicholls State University Portal | STCW Clerk and Sea Project Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help STCW Clerk and Sea Project Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Purpose: The Louisiana Maritime Academy (LMA) at Nicholls State University will start in the Fall of 2028, initially offering a Bachelor of Science in Marine Transportation designed to prepare graduates for the unlimited tonnage third mate merchant mariner credential (MMC). The academic core includes Coast Guard approved maritime courses in addition to fulfilling the general education requirements of Nicholls State University for the Bachelor of Science degree. The position serves as liaison to maritime regulatory agencies and industry partners, processes federal credential and Merchant Mariner Credential applications for all students of LMA, and administers documentation related to Sea Project and the U.S. maritime industry. Special Instructions Nicholls State University adheres to the equal opportunity provisions of federal civil rights laws and regulations that are applicable to this agency. Therefore, no one will be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, national origin (Title VI of the Civil Rights Act of 1964); sex (Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972); disability (Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973; or age (Age Discrimination Act of 1975) in attaining educational goals and objectives and in the administration of personnel policies and procedures. Anyone with questions regarding this policy may contact Alison Hadaway, SHRM -CP, Director of Human Resources at 985-448-4041 / alison.hadaway@nicholls.edu / P.O. Box 2105, Thibodaux, LA 70310. For anyone needing ADA Accommodations, please contact Carolyn Kern, Director of Environmental Health & Safety at 985-448-4782 / carolyn.kern@nicholls.edu Position Details Position Information Position Title STCW Clerk and Sea Project Specialist Position Number 500264 Salary Range $59,000-$66,000 Position Type Unclassified Staff Department Information Ending Effective Date of Temporary Employment Department Office of the President Job Duties Responsibility / Duty General Statement of Duties: The LMA STCW Clerk and Sea Project Specialist will serve as liaison to maritime regulatory agencies and industry partners, processes federal credential and Merchant Mariner Credential applications for all LMA students, and administers documentation related to Sea Projects, sea service and the U.S. maritime industry. Government and Industry Liaison – 50% Serves as liaison to MARAD , the USCG National Maritime Center ( USCG NMC ), and other applicable USCG Divisions in order to remain current with respect to applicable laws, USCG polices, and international treaties which apply to merchant mariner credentialing; continuously seeks ways to improve the Academy&#39;s credentialing processes and ensure a positive rapport with: MARAD , USCG , and NMC . Serves as liaison with Offshore, Towing and Ocean shipping companies, arranging for berths on designated vessels, arranging time and place to board, and providing required information on each cadet. Obtains commercial berths for cadet sea projects, as well as, completes all logistics for cadets assigned sea projects. Academy representative on USCG and MARAD working groups and required to maintain a working relationship with other maritime academy STCW Clerk/ Sea Project staff. Coordinates all interactions with the U.S. Navy’s Military Sealift Command including all logistics for annual recruiting visits. Required to attend annual STCW Coordinator meeting at USCG National Maritime Center. Maintain contact with USCG through the credentialing process. Represent the Maritime Academy at local and national events to establish and strengthen relationships Percentage Of Time 50 Responsibility / Duty Regulatory Approval &amp; Compliance – 40% Processes all cadet applications for USCG merchant mariner credentials and USCG medical certificates, make arrangements for the USCG license exams for senior cadets. Ensures proper documentation is supplied by each cadet per individual company requirements such as physicals, drug tests, immunizations and applications. Oversees all logistical requirements for cadet sea projects. Manage Sea Project homework submission, scans and performs data entry of all documentation (federal documents- TWIC , USCG , Merchant Mariner Credential and USCG health certificate). Ensures all requirements are met prior to issuance of a Merchant Mariner Credential with an officer endorsement (degree audit, no holds, flashing light, etc.). Ensures proper documentation is supplied for each cadet per academy requirements such as registration, insurance coverage, homework assignments plus discharges, letters of recommendation and officer evaluations when cadets return from ships. Percentage Of Time 40 Responsibility / Duty Instructional Quality &amp; Program Assessment – 10% Maintain cadet files in accordance with USCG requirements and ensure they are audit ready. Works closely with the Registrar regarding documentation of USCG and academic graduation requirements. Specifically ensuring new students obtain USCG documents and have internships on commercial vessels. Responsible for ensuring that all cadet internships are with companies that meet U.S. Maritime Administration and LMA Sexual Assault/ Sexual Harassment (SA / SH) policy requirements, and that cadets complete required SA/ SH training prior to departing for an internship on a commercial vessel. May supervise supplemental and student employees as needed. Percentage Of Time 10 Posting Detail Information Minimum Experience Required Between 1-2 years of related maritime experience (Required) Two years of administrative experience (Required) Two years of experience with legal guidelines and policy compliance (Required) Minimum Education Required Minimum Licenses Required Other Minimum Requirements In-depth knowledge of the Merchant Marine Industry (Required) Demonstrated knowledge of STCW requirements, U.S. Coast Guard regulations, and credentialing standards relevant to maritime training. Test(s) Required Preferred Education Bachelor’s Degree (Not Required) Preferred Experience Preferred Licenses Valid Transportation Worker Identification Credential Card obtained in the first 6 months of employment (Required) Notary Public (Not Required) Ability to maintain a database (Required) Ability to maintain individual files for each cadet that are subject to audit (Required) Other Preferred Requirements Physical Demands Employment Year Fiscal Year If Grant Period or Specified Period selected, please specify begin date If Grant Period or Specified Period selected, please specify end date Employment Basis Full-time Proposed Ending Date (for faculty and grant funded positions) Posting Date 09/14/2026 Closing Date 10/13/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Purpose: The Louisiana Maritime Academy ( LMA ) at Nicholls State University will start in the Fall of 2028, initially offering a Bachelor of Science in Marine Transportation designed to prepare graduates for the unlimited tonnage third mate merchant mariner credential ( MMC ). The academic core includes Coast Guard approved maritime courses in addition to fulfilling the general education requirements of Nicholls State University for the Bachelor of Science degree. The position serves as liaison to maritime regulatory agencies and industry partners, processes federal credential and Merchant Mariner Credential applications for all students of LMA , and administers documentation related to Sea Project and the U.S. maritime industry. Quick Link for Postings https://jobs.nicholls.edu/postings/10433 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume/CV Names and Contact Information for a Minimum of THREE References Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Copy of Transcript Optional Documents Other Document 906 East 1st Street, Thibodaux, LA 70301 Back to top Copyright © PeopleAdmin To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.nicholls.edu/postings/10441": {
      "title": "Instructor/Assistant/Associate Professor of Marketing",
      "description": "Nicholls State University Portal | Instructor/Assistant/Associate Professor of Marketing Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Instructor/Assistant/Associate Professor of Marketing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Special Instructions Nicholls State University adheres to the equal opportunity provisions of federal civil rights laws and regulations that are applicable to this agency. Therefore, no one will be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, national origin (Title VI of the Civil Rights Act of 1964); sex (Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972); disability (Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973; or age (Age Discrimination Act of 1975) in attaining educational goals and objectives and in the administration of personnel policies and procedures. Anyone with questions regarding this policy may contact Alison Hadaway, SHRM -CP, Director of Human Resources at 985-448-4041 / alison.hadaway@nicholls.edu / P.O. Box 2105, Thibodaux, LA 70310. For anyone needing ADA Accommodations, please contact Carolyn Kern, Director of Environmental Health & Safety at 985-448-4782 / carolyn.kern@nicholls.edu Position Details Position Information Position Title Instructor/Assistant/Associate Professor of Marketing Position Number 021192 Salary Range Salary is commensurate with education and experience within the institutional pay scale. Position Type Faculty Department Information Ending Effective Date of Temporary Employment Department Management & Marketing Job Duties Responsibility / Duty Delivery of Instruction: At the Instructor level, 12 hours of courses per semester. At the Assistant/Associate level, 9 hours of courses per semester. Effective delivery of student-focused instruction both in the classroom and via online coursework is expected, as is continuous professional improvement and accessibility/interaction with students. Percentage Of Time 55 Responsibility / Duty Scholarly Activity: At the Instructor level, not applicable. At the Assistant/Associate level, successfully publish peer-reviewed journal articles and conference proceedings to maintain academic qualifications. Percentage Of Time 30 Responsibility / Duty Service to Department, College, University, and Community: Participate in student advising, institutional committees, and campus/community/professional activities. Participate in program reviews; participate in student recruitment and retention. Perform other duties as assigned by supervisors. Percentage Of Time 15 Posting Detail Information Minimum Experience Required At the Instructor level, must have significant professional work experience in area of Professional Sales. The professional experience must be of a least 5 years, significant in responsibility, and related to the teaching areas. In addition, the candidate must have strong professionalism and written and oral communication skills. Minimum Education Required At the Instructor level, the individual must hold a Master’s Degree in Marketing or Master’s Degree in Business Administration with a Marketing concentration, or closely related field, preferably from an AACSB accredited school. At the Assistant/Associate level, Ph.D. or D.B. A. in Marketing with Professional Sales interest or related field,preferably from an AACSB accredited school: ABD will be considered, but must provide strong evidence that all Doctoral requirements are completed, less the dissertation. Minimum Licenses Required Other Minimum Requirements Commitment to effective teaching; A strong record of scholarly publication is required for an appointment at the associate professor rank. Test(s) Required N/A Preferred Education N/A Preferred Experience N/A Preferred Licenses N/A Other Preferred Requirements N/A Physical Demands N/A Employment Year Academic Year If Grant Period or Specified Period selected, please specify begin date If Grant Period or Specified Period selected, please specify end date Employment Basis Full-time Proposed Ending Date (for faculty and grant funded positions) 05/15/2027 Posting Date 06/16/2026 Closing Date 11/30/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Postings https://jobs.nicholls.edu/postings/9961 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Teaching Philosophy Names and Contact Information for a Minimum of THREE References Optional Documents Copy of Transcript Other Document 906 East 1st Street, Thibodaux, LA 70301 Back to top Copyright © PeopleAdmin To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.nicholls.edu/postings/10440": {
