lity / Duty Scholarly Activity: At the Instructor level, not applicable. At the Assistant/Associate level, successfully publish peer-reviewed journal articles and conference proceedings to maintain academic qualifications. Percentage Of Time 30 Responsibility / Duty Service to Department, College, University, and Community: Participate in student advising, institutional committees, and campus/community/professional activities. Participate in program reviews; participate in student recruitment and retention. Perform other duties as assigned by supervisors. Percentage Of Time 15 Posting Detail Information Minimum Experience Required At the Instructor level, must have significant professional work experience in the teaching discipline. The professional experience must be of at least 5 years, significant in responsibility, and related to the teaching areas. In addition, the candidate must have strong professionalism and written and oral communication skills. Minimum Education Required At the Instructor level, the individual must hold a Master’s Degree in Management or Master’s Degree in Business Administration with a Management concentration, or closely related field, preferably from an AACSB accredited school. At the Assistant/Associate level, Ph. D. or D.B.A. in Management of related field, preferably from an AACSB accredited school; ABD will be considered, but must provide strong evidence that all Doctoral requirements are completed, less the dissertation. Minimum Licenses Required Other Minimum Requirements Test(s) Required Preferred Education Preferred Experience Demonstrated professional expertise in management with meaningful industry involvement. Teaching experience and industry certifications are a plus. Industry certifications are a plus. Preferred Licenses Other Preferred Requirements Physical Demands Employment Year Academic Year If Grant Period or Specified Period selected, please specify begin date If Grant Period or Specified Period selected, please specify end date Employment Basis Full-time Proposed Ending Date (for faculty and grant funded positions) 05/15/2027 Posting Date 03/10/2026 Closing Date 11/30/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Postings https://jobs.nicholls.edu/postings/9730 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Teaching Philosophy Names and Contact Information for a Minimum of THREE References Copy of Transcript Optional Documents Other Document 906 East 1st Street, Thibodaux, LA 70301 Back to top Copyright © PeopleAdmin To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
