    "https://jobs.nicholls.edu/postings/10451": {
      "title": "Nicholls State University Portal",
      "description": "Nicholls State University Portal | Regional and Transfer Admissions Counselor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Regional and Transfer Admissions Counselor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Special Instructions Nicholls State University adheres to the equal opportunity provisions of federal civil rights laws and regulations that are applicable to this agency. Therefore, no one will be discriminated against on the basis of race, color, national origin (Title VI of the Civil Rights Act of 1964); sex (Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972); disability (Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973; or age (Age Discrimination Act of 1975) in attaining educational goals and objectives and in the administration of personnel policies and procedures. Anyone with questions regarding this policy may contact Alison Hadaway, SHRM -CP, Director of Human Resources at 985-448-4041 / alison.hadaway@nicholls.edu / P.O. Box 2105, Thibodaux, LA 70310. For anyone needing ADA Accommodations, please contact Carolyn Kern, Director of Environmental Health & Safety at 985-448-4782 / carolyn.kern@nicholls.edu Position Details Position Information Position Title Regional and Transfer Admissions Counselor Position Number 500266 Salary Range $45,000.00-$50,000.00 Position Type Unclassified Staff Department Information Ending Effective Date of Temporary Employment Department Enrollment Services Job Duties Responsibility / Duty Regional Territory Management and Recruitment, 45% Manage an assigned regional recruitment territory, emphasizing strategic out-of-state enrollment growth. Support university recruitment efforts in targeted markets that may include East Texas, the Mississippi Gulf Coast, South Alabama, the Florida Panhandle, and other markets identified through the Strategic Enrollment Plan. Develop, execute, and manage a data-informed recruitment plan for the assigned territory, identifying high-potential schools, communities, organizations, and recruitment events. Represent Nicholls at college fairs, high school visits, community college events, regional recruitment programs, and other enrollment activities. Build year-round relationships with school counselors, college advisors, students, families, alumni, community organizations, and other regional partners. Identify emerging markets and recruitment opportunities using enrollment trends, inquiry data, application data, demographic information, and previous recruitment results. Develop strategies for increasing awareness of Nicholls in markets where the university has historically had limited visibility. Work independently while traveling within the assigned territory and maintain consistent communication with the Director of Admissions and Admissions team. Coordinate travel schedules, fair registrations, school visits, regional events, and recruitment expenses within established university guidelines. Percentage Of Time 45 Responsibility / Duty Transfer Recruitment and Pipeline Development, 25% Develop, execute, and manage a comprehensive recruitment strategy for prospective transfer students. Establish and maintain relationships with community colleges, technical colleges, and other institutions that represent potential transfer pipelines for Nicholls. Conduct regular visits to community colleges and participate in transfer fairs, advising events, classroom visits, college events, and other recruitment opportunities. Develop relationships with community college advisors, faculty, administrators, and student organizations to increase awareness of transfer opportunities at Nicholls. Identify high-potential institutions and programs for targeted transfer recruitment based on enrollment data, academic alignment, geography, and student mobility patterns. Work collaboratively with academic departments and enrollment partners to communicate transfer pathways, articulation opportunities, degree options, and career outcomes. Assist prospective transfer students in understanding admissions requirements, enrollment deadlines, transfer credit processes, financial aid, scholarships, and next steps. Develop and manage targeted strategies to reengage students with existing college credit who have discontinued their enrollment or are exploring opportunities to continue their education at another institution. Coordinate transfer-focused recruitment events, information sessions, virtual programs, and campus visit opportunities. Monitor transfer inquiry, application, admission, and enrollment trends, and recommend strategies to improve transfer conversion. Percentage Of Time 25 Responsibility / Duty Prospective Student Counseling and Yield Management, 20% Provide personalized enrollment counseling to prospective students and families throughout the recruitment and enrollment process. Develop relationships with inquiries, prospects, applicants, admitted students, and deposited or oriented students to encourage progression through the enrollment funnel. Conduct individual appointments, phone calls, virtual meetings, presentations, campus visits, and other recruitment interactions. Assist students with understanding admissions requirements, application procedures, financial aid and scholarship opportunities, housing, orientation, academic programs, campus resources, and enrollment deadlines. Identify barriers preventing admitted students from enrolling and work collaboratively with appropriate university offices to help students resolve them. Implement targeted yield strategies for transfer students and students within assigned regional markets. Conduct appropriate follow-up with students who have incomplete applications, missing enrollment requirements, or other outstanding steps. Provide responsive, professional, and student-centered communication to students and families. Percentage Of Time 20 Responsibility / Duty Other Responsibilities as Needed – 10% Requires the ability to drive to recruiting programs/events. Overnight travel required. Requires the ability to transport, load, set up, and break down recruiting materials. Occasional lifting and carrying of boxes, materials, signage, and equipment as needed. Percentage Of Time 10 Posting Detail Information Minimum Experience Required Minimum Education Required Bachelor’s Degree Minimum Licenses Required Other Minimum Requirements Exceptional communication skills. Ability to be self-directed and manage multiple priorities. Test(s) Required Preferred Education Preferred Experience Marketing, public relations, or sales experience preferred. College admissions background preferred. Preferred Licenses Other Preferred Requirements Physical Demands Requires the ability to drive to recruiting programs/events. Overnight travel required. Requires the ability to transport, load, set up, and break down recruiting materials. Occasional lifting and carrying of boxes, materials, signage, and equipment as needed. Employment Year Fiscal Year If Grant Period or Specified Period selected, please specify begin date If Grant Period or Specified Period selected, please specify end date Employment Basis Full-time Proposed Ending Date (for faculty and grant funded positions) Posting Date 09/18/2026 Closing Date 10/18/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Postings https://jobs.nicholls.edu/postings/10450 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Names and Contact Information for a Minimum of THREE References Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Copy of Transcript Optional Documents Other Document 906 East 1st Street, Thibodaux, LA 70301 Back to top Copyright © PeopleAdmin To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
